<title>UK: Fire destroys part-cargo of flour for Libya.</title>
<headline>Fire destroys part-cargo of flour for Libya.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 2,600 tonnes of flour on board the Liberian-flag vessel Captain P. were destroyed by a fire at Boulogne, France, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The 10,975 dwt vessel arrived at Boulogne on May 15 to load 10,500 tonnes of flour for Libya. A fire broke out in the forward hold on May 20 and local fire crews extinguished the blaze.</p>
<p>The cargo in the forward hold was destroyed.</p>
</text>
